    "description": "Navigate and read Hugging Face Hub resources using filesystem-style commands (ls, cat, find, stat, search) over hf:// URIs. Returns structured listings, file contents, metadata, or search results.\n\nUse `hub_repo_search` instead for interactive repo discovery by query. Use `hub_repo_details` instead for structured dataset structure/preview. Use `hf_fs` for raw file access, documentation, papers, collections, buckets, or when you need fine-grained path control.\n\nRoots: hf://models, hf://datasets, hf://spaces, hf://buckets, hf://collections, hf://papers, hf://docs\n\nCommands and key usage:\n- `ls URI` — list contents; use hf://models/trending, hf://datasets/trending, hf://spaces/trending, or hf://papers/trending for trending items (up to 20)\n- `cat URI [RELATIVE_PATH]` — read a file; supports --offset and --max-bytes for partial reads\n- `stat URI [RELATIVE_PATH]` — get metadata for a single resource\n- `find URI` — recursive search with optional --name/--glob, --path, and --type filters\n- `search URI QUERY` — semantic or keyword search; valid roots: hf://models, hf://datasets, hf://spaces (semantic), hf://collections, hf://docs scopes, hf://papers (all require a query except collection/model/dataset/space browsing)\n\nParameters:\n- cmd: One of ls, cat, find, stat, search\n- args: Array of string tokens forming the command arguments (each flag and value is a separate element)\n\nNotes: No shell pipes, redirects, or expansion. Multiple QUERY tokens are joined with spaces. Use hf://docs to find documentation; ls hf://docs to list products, then follow returned URIs. For papers, ls hf://papers/ARXIV_ID then cat the .md or metadata.json. Use --kind mcp with search on hf://spaces to filter for MCP servers.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "args": {
          "description": "Command arguments; each array item is one grammar token.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "cmd": {
          "description": "Command to execute.",
          "enum": [
            "ls",
            "cat",
            "stat",
            "find",
            "search"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "cmd",
        "args"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "hf:hf_fs"
  },
